1.4 The house of answers
While the QCC should prove useful for evaluating a characterization of cognition, they are not obviously useful for directing such a characterization. Instead, I think we need to turn to specifying a few central questions that have arisen in the last 50 years of cognitive science research. As a result, in this section I suggest four questions which, if answered in detail, should go a long way to providing a characterization of a cognitive system that addresses most, if not all, of the QCC. These questions are:


