Running a model
You want to make sure your model works, so you need to use to the parts of Nengo that let you ‘run’ the model. There are two ways to run models in Nengo. The first is a ‘non-interactive mode’, which lets you put ‘probes’ into parts of the network. You then run the network for some length of time, and those probes gather data (such as when neurons are active, what their internal currents and voltages are, etc.). You can then view that information later using the built in data


